<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Model fidelity to source: 56/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates a 1D rectified cosine approximation of primary siphonal canal spines (L31-69), but lacks a Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica + unilateral foundation solver, omits tubular base closure (gamma >= gamma_fold) vs open-gutter flaring, omits 2-stage and 3-stage secondary/tertiary fractal frond serrations (*Chicoreus ramosus*), omits episodic triradiate varix whorl accretion, and lacks an explicit subcritical negative control evaluation in `measure_morphoeval()`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L31–L69: Single-generation 1D cosine approximation without Kirchhoff elastica loop solver, multi-stage fronding, or episodic varix cycle <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L31-L69>" ;
    pk:hasScore 5.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

