<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-3> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) Multi-Generational Fractal Fronding Wavenumber Cascade" ;
    dct:description "Proves that distal thinning of an already buckled primary spine crest reduces flexural rigidity D_i ~ E h_i^3, cascading the instability to higher wavenumbers k_2^*/k_1^* ≈ 3.8 and k_3^* > k_2^* to form secondary and tertiary fractal frond serrations in Chicoreus ramosus | Variables: h_1, h_2, h_3: primary, secondary, and tertiary distal mantle margin thicknesses (mm); K_s: unilateral calcified shell foundation stiffness (MPa/mm); E: mantle Young's modulus (MPa); k_i^*: characteristic buckling wavenumber (mm^-1)" ;
    dct:source "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) J. Theor. Biol. 364:420-430 Sec. 3-4 & Figs. 5-8" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L140-L315>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_077_mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling.lean#L21-L55> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def frond_wavenumber_residual (E_h3 k4 K_s : Int) : Int :=
  E_h3 * k4 - 3 * K_s
def frond_cascade_gap (h_coarse h_fine : Int) : Int :=
  h_coarse * h_coarse * h_coarse - h_fine * h_fine * h_fine
theorem moulton_secondary_frond_cascade (E_h3 K_s : Int) :
    frond_wavenumber_residual E_h3 (3 * K_s) (E_h3 * K_s) = 0 ∧
    frond_cubic_thickness 1 < frond_cubic_thickness 2 ∧
    frond_cubic_thickness 2 < frond_cubic_thickness 6 ∧
    frond_cascade_gap 6 1 = 215 ∧
    frond_cascade_gap 6 2 = 208
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_i^* = (3 K_s / (E h_i^3))^(1/4);  h_3 < h_2 < h_1  ⇒  k_3^* > k_2^* > k_1^*,  k_2^* / k_1^* = (h_1 / h_2)^(3/4) ≈ 3.8" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.09.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff-Clebsch Elastica on Unilateral Foundation & Hierarchical Multi-Stage Mantle Spine Buckling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_077.frond_cascade_gap" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_077.moulton_secondary_frond_cascade" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) Tubular vs Open-Gutter Spine Folding Closure Criterion" ;
    dct:description "Governs the topological transition from an open-gutter spine or flared frond apex (γ_c < γ < γ_fold, Chicoreus distal frond) to a self-contacting sealed hollow tubular spine (γ ≥ γ_fold, Murex pecten siphonal comb spines) | Variables: γ: incremental circumferential mantle growth stretch; γ_c: critical buckling stretch threshold; γ_fold: elastica self-contact folding threshold; Δx_neck: basal neck opening width (mm)" ;
    dct:source "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) J. Theor. Biol. 364:420-430 Sec. 2.2-3.1 & Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) PNAS 110:6015-6020 Fig. 3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L210-L395>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_077_mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling.lean#L61-L90> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def spine_neck_gap (w_base gamma_fold gamma : Int) : Int :=
  w_base * (gamma_fold - gamma)
def is_tubular_sealed (w_base gamma_fold gamma : Int) : Bool :=
  decide (spine_neck_gap w_base gamma_fold gamma ≤ 0)
theorem moulton_tubular_spine_closure_criterion (w_base gamma_fold : Int) :
    spine_neck_gap w_base gamma_fold gamma_fold = 0 ∧
    spine_neck_gap 4 142 130 = 48 ∧
    is_tubular_sealed 4 142 130 = false ∧
    is_tubular_sealed 4 142 142 = true ∧
    spine_neck_gap 4 142 168 = -104 ∧
    is_tubular_sealed 4 142 168 = true
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δx_neck(γ) = w_base (1 - (γ - γ_c)/(γ_fold - γ_c));  γ ≥ γ_fold ⇔ Δx_neck(γ) ≤ 0 (tubular base closure)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.09.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff-Clebsch Elastica on Unilateral Foundation & Hierarchical Multi-Stage Mantle Spine Buckling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_077.spine_neck_gap" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_077.moulton_tubular_spine_closure_criterion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Episodic Triradiate Varix Rest-Period Spine Periodicity & Subcritical Smooth Whorl Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that subcritical inter-varix mantle growth (γ ≤ γ_c) yields smooth unspined shell whorls while periodic rest-period growth bursts every Δφ = 120° produce three phase-locked triradiate spine rows per whorl | Variables: φ: helicospiral whorl accretion angle (deg); γ(φ): episodic mantle growth profile; γ_c: critical buckling threshold; A_spine: radial spine outgrowth amplitude (mm); Δφ_varix = 120°: angular spacing between successive varices" ;
    dct:source "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) PNAS 110:6015-6020 pp. 6016-6019 & Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2012) J. Theor. Biol. 311:69-79" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L400-L485>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_077_mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling.lean#L96-L125> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def episodic_varix_amplitude_sq (A0_sq gamma gamma_c : Nat) : Nat :=
  A0_sq * (gamma - gamma_c)
def triradiate_whorl_period_deg (n_varices_per_whorl delta_phi_deg : Nat) : Nat :=
  n_varices_per_whorl * delta_phi_deg
theorem moulton_episodic_varix_rest_period (A0_sq gamma_c dgamma : Nat) :
    episodic_varix_amplitude_sq A0_sq gamma_c gamma_c = 0 ∧
    episodic_varix_amplitude_sq A0_sq 0 gamma_c = 0 ∧
    episodic_varix_amplitude_sq A0_sq (gamma_c + (dgamma + 1)) gamma_c = A0_sq * (dgamma + 1) ∧
    triradiate_whorl_period_deg 3 120 = 360
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "A_spine^2(γ) = A_0^2 max(0, γ(φ) - γ_c);  γ(φ) ≤ γ_c ⇒ A_spine = 0 (smooth inter-varix whorl);  3 Δφ_varix = 360° (Δφ_varix = 120°)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.09.021>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff-Clebsch Elastica on Unilateral Foundation & Hierarchical Multi-Stage Mantle Spine Buckling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_077.episodic_varix_amplitude_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_077.moulton_episodic_varix_rest_period" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "MorphoEval simulation-faithfulness rubric v0.1.0" ;
    dct:description "Weighted 0-100 rubric for the faithfulness of a morphology simulation to its organism and source model; Overall = weighted mean. Each score is a pk:LLMClaimAssessment (ProbKnow rubric-assessment template) of the pk:Claim pkr:claim/morphoeval-<sim> against one dimension (dct:subject the dimension concept, pk:assessmentType morphoeval/<version>/<dimension>) with pk:hasScore = score/100 — an uncalibrated rubric score, not a probability — and a pk:hasVerdict band; the overall score has the rubric itself as dct:subject and is also the pk:weightOfEvidence of the claim." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/rubric.yaml> ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> .

